        "title": "Population and Urban Geography",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Demography is destiny — population size, age structure, and distribution shape\neverything from labor markets to geopolitical power. The demographic transition\nmodel describes where every country has been or is heading. Urbanization is the\ndominant spatial process of the 21st century — more people now live in cities\nthan outside them for the first time in human history. Understanding Zipf's Law,\nmegacity formation, and the mechanics of migration ties human geography directly\nto economic and political geography."
